  "content": {
    "id": "p6-q26-task",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Jane leaves her campsite and hikes due west $12\\text{ km}$ and then $4\\text{ km}$ due south. Give true bearings correct to the nearest degree, using three digits.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p6-q26-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "What is the bearing of Jane from the campsite?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$252^\\circ$",
          "worked": "Let $\\alpha$ be the angle south of west from the campsite to Jane.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\alpha&=\\frac{4}{12}\\\\\\alpha&=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{4}{12}\\right)\\\\\\text{Bearing}&=270^\\circ-\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{4}{12}\\right)\\\\\\text{Bearing}&\\approx252^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe bearing is $252^\\circ$, to the nearest degree.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q26-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What is the bearing of the campsite from Jane?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$072^\\circ$",
          "worked": "Use the unrounded bearing from part (a).\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Reverse bearing}&=270^\\circ-\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{4}{12}\\right)-180^\\circ\\\\\\text{Reverse bearing}&=90^\\circ-\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{4}{12}\\right)\\\\\\text{Reverse bearing}&\\approx72^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\n\nWritten using three digits, the bearing is $072^\\circ$, to the nearest degree.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
    ]
  },
